Classic Github InstallerThe saved VISE project contains the FAT application, login helper,Read Me and license notices. Color and monochrome splash screens andinstallation billboards are embedded in the project. The editable PICTfiles and artwork resource file are in this folder.BUILD1. Use a licensed Installer VISE 6 setup that permits redistribution.   The evaluation builder marks its output UNLICENSED; do not publish it.   Open Classic Github.vct.2. If the application was rebuilt, choose Archive > Bring Up To Date.   Review and update the changed application before saving the project.3. Choose File > Build Installer. Use Single File as the target.4. Save as Install Github Classic in the repository's Output:Installer   folder, replacing the previous installer there when appropriate.5. Test the installer in a separate folder. Keep the app and helper together.6. Compress Output:Installer with DropStuff. Rename the resulting archive   Install Github Classic.sit and move it to the repository root,   replacing the previous installer archive when appropriate.The application is also available in Output and GitHubClassic-0.2.sit.The source payloads use their original Macintosh locations. If this projectwas cloned elsewhere, reselect the matching sources when VISE asks.The Read Me setting refers to the Read Me in this folder.Version 0.2 ships as Output:GitHubClassic-0.2.sit. The root installer archiveand Output:Installer still contain the older 0.1 release. The refreshedproject and artwork are ready for a licensed installer build.Keep the Macintosh date and time correct for HTTPS certificate validation.